$$d(x_m,x_n)=\sqrt{\left(1-0\right)^2+\left(0-1\right)^2}=2.$$

Therefore, for any subsequence $\{x_{n_k}\}$ of $\{x_n\}$, we have

$$d^{*}(x_{n_k},x_{n_l}) \geq 2.$$

This shows that $\{x_n\}$ does not have a convergent subsequence, and therefore $S$ is not compact.

